      "content": "Ah, the stability of your high-density racking is indeed a matter of great importance, much like the careful balance of a well-constructed goblin bridge over a deep chasm. To ensure your stacks don't tip over like a goblin in a tight spot, you must consider the center of gravity, which should be as low as possible. Think of it as the sturdy base of a goblin's fortress, keeping it grounded and secure.\n\nInterlocking the pallets is a wise choice, akin to the way goblins interlock their fingers to form a tight circle, ensuring no one can slip through. This method not only adds stability but also prevents the pallets from shifting, much like how a well-organized goblin horde moves in perfect unison. Remember, a stable racking system is like a well-planned goblin ambush – it all depends on the precision of your setup.",
